<%# /contests — three bands, each answering a different question:

      1. the featured rail   what can I play right now?
      2. My Contests         where do I stand in the ones I'm in?
      3. All Contests        the full list.

    The whole page shares one Alpine scope so the admin Show Settled toggle
    controls the All Contests table from the section header it now sits in.
    showSettled starts false: settled contests are hidden there by default for
    everyone (admins and non-admins alike), and only the admin-only toggle can
    flip it. Single-quote everything inside x-data to avoid breaking the
    double-quoted attribute.

    MY CONTESTS DOES NOT ANSWER TO THAT TOGGLE. A settled contest is the one
    thing that band exists to report on — the Won / Complete badge and the
    amount won have no meaning before a contest ends — so it always shows its
    settled rows. See contests/_contest_table's `hide_settled`. %>
<div x-data="{ showSettled: false }">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-heading mb-6">Contests</h1>

  <%# ===== The featured rail — open contests first, then coming soon, each
      band newest-first (Contest.featured_order). It carries NO heading: it is
      the top of the page and it is the page's headline, so a label above it
      would only push the contests themselves down. ===== %>
  <% if @featured_contests.any? %>
    <section class="mb-10" x-data="contestRail()" data-contest-band="featured">
      <%# The mask is the house's overflow idiom (shared/_alpine_factories
          contestRail, and navUsernameFade before it): taper the content itself
          rather than paint a gradient that would have to know the page's
          background colour. It is bound, not static, so a rail that fits on
          screen is not given a fade that lies about more cards to the right. %>
      <div x-ref="viewport"
           data-contest-rail
           <%# `py-5` rather than `pb-2`: `overflow-x-auto` forces overflow-y to
               a non-visible value, so the rail box CLIPS anything a card throws
               past its own top or bottom edge — and the fizz's whole point is
               the bubbles that escape. The padding is the room they escape
               INTO. Take it away and the carbonation ends at the card's edge,
               which is the one place it must not. %>
           class="tt-contest-rail overflow-x-auto overflow-y-hidden py-5"
           @scroll.passive="measure()"
           x-bind:style="canScrollRight ? '-webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, black 85%, transparent); mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, black 85%, transparent);' : ''">
        <div class="flex gap-4 items-stretch">
          <%# 320 / 384px, a step up from 288 / 320. THE BANNER IS WHY. It is a
              5:1 crop shown in a fixed-height `object-cover` box, so the box's
              WIDTH is the only thing that decides how much of the art survives
              the crop: at 320px the card kept 2.2 of the image's 5 widths, at
              384px it keeps 2.7 — a fifth more banner, from the same stored
              image, with no re-crop. The card grew with it rather than the
              banner alone, so the proportions the rest of the card was tuned at
              hold. %>
          <%# THE FIZZ LIVES OUT HERE, NOT IN THE CARD. The card is
              `overflow-hidden` — it has to be, that is what clips the sash into
              a corner ribbon — so bubbles rendered inside it would be cut off
              at exactly the edges they exist to cross. This wrapper is the
              engine's `.hold-stack` (studio/_fizz_layer, engine-motion.css):
              it positions the bubble layer across the card and z-orders it
              BEHIND, so the carbonation shows only where it escapes.

              Coming-soon cards get no layer at all — the same line the hover
              lift draws. A contest that is not playable yet should not be the
              liveliest thing on the page. %>
          <% @featured_contests.each do |contest| %>
            <div class="w-80 sm:w-96 flex-shrink-0 hold-stack tt-contest-stack"
                 data-contest-stack="<%= contest.slug %>">
              <% unless contest.coming_soon? %>
                <%# Seeded on the slug, so a contest's bubbles are the same
                    scatter on every render (Turbo restores a cached page into
                    the same markup) and two cards on one rail differ. %>
                <%= render "studio/fizz_layer", seed: contest.slug %>
              <% end %>
              <%= render "contests/contest_card",
                         contest: contest,
                         entry_count: @entry_counts[contest.id] || 0,
                         my_entry_count: @my_entry_counts[contest.id] || 0 %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  <% end %>

  <%# ===== My Contests — every contest this viewer is in or has been part of,
      finished ones included. Hidden entirely for guests and for anyone with no
      entries. ===== %>
  <% if logged_in? && @my_contests.any? %>
    <section class="mb-10" data-contest-band="mine">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">My Contests</h2>
        <%= link_to "View all →", my_contests_path, class: "text-sm text-primary hover:underline" %>
      </div>

      <%= render "contests/contest_table",
                 contests: @my_contests,
                 entry_counts: @entry_counts,
                 entered_contest_ids: @entered_contest_ids,
                 payouts: @my_payout_cents,
                 hide_settled: false %>
    </section>
  <% end %>

  <%# ===== All Contests — the full list, and the home of the two controls that
      act on it. Show Settled filters this table; New Contest adds to it. Both
      are admin-only: contest creation is gated server-side (ContestsController
      #new/#create require_admin), and settled contests stay hidden for
      everyone else because only this button can reveal them. ===== %>
  <section data-contest-band="all">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">All Contests</h2>
      <% if current_user&.admin? %>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <%# Style flips on state: muted outline when OFF, filled accent when
              ON, so it reads as secondary to the green New Contest CTA. %>
          <button type="button"
                  @click="showSettled = !showSettled"
                  :class="showSettled ? 'btn btn-secondary' : 'btn btn-outline'"
                  :aria-pressed="showSettled"
                  x-text="showSettled ? 'Hide Settled' : 'Show Settled'">Show Settled</button>
          <%= link_to "New Contest", new_contest_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <% if @contests.any? %>
      <%= render "contests/contest_table",
                 contests: @contests,
                 entry_counts: @entry_counts,
                 entered_contest_ids: @entered_contest_ids,
                 payouts: nil,
                 hide_settled: true %>

      <%# Empty state: every contest in the list is settled, so the table
          renders no visible rows with the toggle OFF. Show a subtle note
          (revealed away once settled are shown). %>
      <% if @contests.all?(&:settled?) %>
        <p x-show="!showSettled" class="text-secondary mt-3">No open contests right now.</p>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <p class="text-secondary">No contests yet.</p>
    <% end %>
  </section>
</div>
